messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/list.c
Line: 1125
Function: list_objects
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: The code calls strcmp(sn, ln) where sn is obtained via OBJ_nid2sn(i) and may be NULL. Passing a NULL pointer to strcmp causes a crash. Subsequently, sn is also printed with %s at lines 1126/1128 without checking for NULL, leading to the same issue for objects that have only a long name or lack a short name.

Source context:
```c
     1085: {
     1086:     int max_nid = OBJ_new_nid(0);
     1087:     int i;
     1088:     char *oid_buf = NULL;
     1089:     int oid_size = 0;
     1090: 
     1091:     /* Skip 0, since that's NID_undef */
     1092:     for (i = 1; i < max_nid; i++) {
     1093:         const ASN1_OBJECT *obj = OBJ_nid2obj(i);
     1094:         const char *sn = OBJ_nid2sn(i);
     1095:         const char *ln = OBJ_nid2ln(i);
     1096:         int n = 0;
